1
00:00:05,251 --> 00:00:11,372
On the night of 11 June 1962, three
men left their cells at Alcatraz,

2
00:00:11,663 --> 00:00:14,859
the federal prison on an
island in San Francisco Bay.

3
00:00:17,151 --> 00:00:18,124
At the morning count,

4
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:21,859
three beds held something that
only looked like a sleeping man.

5
00:00:24,171 --> 00:00:25,744
More than sixty years later,

6
00:00:25,834 --> 00:00:29,312
the Bureau of Prisons still lists them
as missing and presumed drowned.

7
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:32,639
This is what the record
shows, and where it stops.

8
00:00:40,211 --> 00:00:44,792
Alcatraz was a federal
prison from 1934 to 1963,

9
00:00:45,183 --> 00:00:47,399
on a small island in
San Francisco Bay.

10
00:00:49,831 --> 00:00:52,913
The Bureau of Prisons counts
fourteen escape attempts there,

11
00:00:53,064 --> 00:00:54,298
by thirty-six men.

12
00:00:56,611 --> 00:00:57,766
Twenty-three were caught.

13
00:00:58,118 --> 00:00:59,393
Six were shot and killed.

14
00:00:59,665 --> 00:01:00,498
Two drowned.

15
00:01:02,851 --> 00:01:05,846
Officially, no one ever
succeeded in escaping.

16
00:01:06,257 --> 00:01:09,213
Five men are listed as missing
and presumed drowned,

17
00:01:09,484 --> 00:01:12,119
and three of them left in June 1962.

18
00:01:22,471 --> 00:01:26,509
An Associated Press story from
1962 counted eleven attempts,

19
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:27,521
not fourteen.

20
00:01:27,541 --> 00:01:31,679
The counts differ, and this video
uses the Bureau's later number.

21
00:01:33,951 --> 00:01:37,850
The three were Frank Morris, and the
brothers John and Clarence Anglin.

22
00:01:38,202 --> 00:01:41,279
The Associated Press described
all three as bank robbers.

23
00:01:43,551 --> 00:01:46,407
Morris came to Alcatraz
in January 1960.

24
00:01:46,758 --> 00:01:51,859
John Anglin arrived that October, and
Clarence followed in January 1961.

25
00:01:54,271 --> 00:01:55,598
Clarence already had a record

26
00:01:55,618 --> 00:01:58,058
of four escapes from
Florida prison work gangs.

27
00:02:00,311 --> 00:02:03,708
The AP reported that
Morris had an IQ of 132.

28
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:06,354
An official of the Bureau
of Prisons said of him:

29
00:02:06,665 --> 00:02:08,299
"Above all, he's a planner."

30
00:02:23,851 --> 00:02:26,958
The plan began at the back of
their cells, with the air vents.

31
00:02:29,211 --> 00:02:33,073
The FBI says the men drilled closely
spaced holes around the vents,

32
00:02:33,224 --> 00:02:34,598
until the covers came free.

33
00:02:37,152 --> 00:02:40,238
Newspapers at the time said the
tools were sharpened spoons.

34
00:02:42,610 --> 00:02:46,708
Behind the cells ran a utility corridor,
where the prison kept its pipes.

35
00:02:47,299 --> 00:02:49,293
According to an AP photo caption,

36
00:02:49,784 --> 00:02:52,639
towels and a robe hid the
hole in John Anglin's cell.

37
00:03:03,092 --> 00:03:05,117
In their beds, they left dummy heads.

38
00:03:07,451 --> 00:03:10,200
The FBI says the heads
were made of plaster,

39
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,859
flesh-tone paint, and real human hair.

40
00:03:15,191 --> 00:03:19,399
After the escape, a guard pushed one
of them off a bed, and its nose broke.

41
00:03:21,591 --> 00:03:22,724
Then came the raft.

42
00:03:23,115 --> 00:03:26,194
The FBI describes it as
six feet by fourteen,

43
00:03:26,284 --> 00:03:28,179
made from more than fifty raincoats.

44
00:03:30,331 --> 00:03:31,644
The seams were stitched,

45
00:03:32,015 --> 00:03:34,531
and sealed with heat from
the prison's steam pipes.

46
00:03:35,082 --> 00:03:37,759
The men also made wooden
paddles and life preservers.

47
00:03:40,291 --> 00:03:43,248
A fourth inmate, Allen
West, was part of the plan.

48
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:47,579
His vent was not fully open, and he
was still in his cell the next morning.

49
00:03:49,791 --> 00:03:54,314
In 1979, the film Escape from
Alcatraz dramatized this plan,

50
00:03:54,404 --> 00:03:56,319
with Clint Eastwood as Frank Morris.

51
00:03:58,451 --> 00:04:00,286
The next scenes come from that film.

52
00:04:00,778 --> 00:04:04,558
They show actors, not the real
men, and not the real night.

53
00:04:36,071 --> 00:04:37,526
On Monday, 11 June,

54
00:04:38,039 --> 00:04:40,679
the three men were last seen
at nine thirty in the evening.

55
00:04:42,931 --> 00:04:45,929
They were found missing at a
quarter past seven the next morning,

56
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,359
which gave them a head start
of about nine and a half hours.

57
00:04:51,891 --> 00:04:55,622
Acting Warden Arthur Dollison said it
appeared they had gone into the bay

58
00:04:55,642 --> 00:04:56,314
on a raft,

59
00:04:56,525 --> 00:04:57,899
or on pieces of driftwood.

60
00:05:00,311 --> 00:05:03,050
The prison said they had gone
through the utility tunnel,

61
00:05:03,281 --> 00:05:05,619
up to the roof, and down
a pipe to the water.

62
00:05:16,011 --> 00:05:19,631
San Francisco police, the FBI, and
the Coast Guard searched the bay.

63
00:05:20,283 --> 00:05:22,259
Soldiers searched
nearby Angel Island.

64
00:05:25,515 --> 00:05:25,495
Within two days,

65
00:05:25,515 --> 00:05:28,939
investigators recovered a packet
of letters sealed in rubber.

66
00:05:31,271 --> 00:05:34,310
Pieces of wood that looked like
paddles were found in the water.

67
00:05:34,821 --> 00:05:37,458
A homemade life vest washed
up on Cronkhite Beach.

68
00:05:39,971 --> 00:05:43,431
Weeks later, a body in blue
clothing was found up the coast.

69
00:05:44,003 --> 00:05:45,839
It was too decayed to identify.

70
00:05:56,271 --> 00:05:59,927
Warden Olin Blackwell said he did
not believe the men were alive,

71
00:06:00,118 --> 00:06:01,350
if they had tried to swim.

72
00:06:02,082 --> 00:06:04,536
But officials conceded that
they could have reached shore

73
00:06:04,687 --> 00:06:05,879
on a makeshift raft.

74
00:06:08,431 --> 00:06:10,688
A newspaper report
suggested outside help.

75
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:13,919
The FBI later said it found no proof of it.

76
00:06:21,091 --> 00:06:23,858
The FBI worked the case
for seventeen years.

77
00:06:26,231 --> 00:06:29,507
Its conclusion was that the
men likely did not survive.

78
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:32,593
It pointed to the strong
currents and cold water,

79
00:06:32,703 --> 00:06:35,919
and to the lack of any credible
evidence that they were alive.

80
00:06:38,131 --> 00:06:40,867
The FBI closed its case in 1979.

81
00:06:41,458 --> 00:06:44,285
Today, the US Marshals
Service is the agency

82
00:06:44,305 --> 00:06:46,319
that still lists the men as fugitives.

83
00:06:48,771 --> 00:06:51,830
In 2013, a letter reached
San Francisco police.

84
00:06:52,502 --> 00:06:54,698
It claimed to be from John Anglin.

85
00:06:57,151 --> 00:06:59,758
The writer said he was
eighty-three and had cancer.

86
00:06:59,778 --> 00:07:03,619
He wrote: "Yes we all made
it that night but barely!"

87
00:07:05,931 --> 00:07:07,507
He offered to say where he was,

88
00:07:07,758 --> 00:07:10,479
if he were promised a short
jail term and medical care.

89
00:07:12,711 --> 00:07:14,675
The letter became public in 2018.

90
00:07:14,695 --> 00:07:19,113
The FBI tested it for fingerprints,
DNA and handwriting.

91
00:07:19,645 --> 00:07:22,039
The results, it said, were inconclusive.

92
00:07:24,451 --> 00:07:26,568
According to CBS San Francisco,

93
00:07:26,679 --> 00:07:29,579
the Marshals considered the
lead closed, and without merit.

94
00:07:31,791 --> 00:07:36,278
In 2017, a deputy marshal said it was
more likely that they did not make it.

95
00:07:38,812 --> 00:07:42,618
As of the latest reports, the Marshals
Service has not closed the file.

96
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:55,696
So the record holds a letter
that no test could confirm,

97
00:07:55,716 --> 00:07:58,061
and a body that no one could identify.

98
00:07:58,081 --> 00:08:02,339
It holds no proof that they lived,
and no proof that they died.

99
00:08:04,691 --> 00:08:07,918
Did the bay keep them, or did
they walk away from the Rock?
